    "result_text": "Full build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented a derived `timezone` field on the owner response, derived from the locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `REGION_TIMEZONE` lookup table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `getTimezone()` getter that derives the IANA name from the existing `getLocality()` region, returning `null` (field omitted) when the locality maps to no known region.\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `timezone` property to the Owner response schema (right after `locality`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct auto-maps it by name from `Owner.getTimezone()`.\n\nThis follows the codebase's existing pattern for derived owner fields (`locality`, `checkDigit`, `ageBand`, etc.) \u2014 entity getter \u2192 OpenAPI schema \u2192 MapStruct name-matched mapping \u2014 rather than adding a new OfficeFloor function step, since timezone is a pure per-response derivation off already-stored state.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` passes (Sydney/postcode 2000 \u2192 locality `NSW`, timezone `Australia/Sydney`), and the full `./mvnw test` build is green.",
